    cof:title "31(3) December were a reference to the last day of the 6-month" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) The Commissioner may revoke the decision if satisfied that a condition has not been complied with.  Responsibilities of registered entities  Chapter 3 Record keeping and reporting  Part 3-2 Reporting  Division 60 Section 60-95 Australian Charities and Not-for-profits Commission Act 2012 Compilation date: 05/12/2025 Subdivision 60-G—Collective and joint reporting 60-95  Commissioner may approve collective or joint reporting by related entities Joint reporting" ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer .

concept:australian-charities-and-not-for-profits-commission-act-2012-sec-31-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31(1) December were a reference to the last day of the 6-month"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sec-31-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Commissioner may allow 2 or more registered entities (reporting group) to prepare and lodge a single information statement, or a single information statement and a single financial report, in relation to the reporting group for a financial year. Collective reporting" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Commissioner may allow 2 or more registered entities (reporting group) to prepare and lodge a single information statement, or a single information statement and a single financial report, in relation to the reporting group for a financial year. Collective reporting"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "018ddb50860c606374645e96d6ef787275984e69dd6abb400cac079039c4c132" ;
    values:partOf concept:australian-charities-and-not-for-profits-commission-act-2012-sec-31 ;
    cof:pageNumber "62"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Commissioner may impose conditions on a decision to allow adoption of an accounting period. Commissioner allows registered entities to prepare and lodge a single information statement or financial report." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
